  explanation = $EXPL$Correct (C): Under IRC Sec. 2702, the taxable gift for a qualified personal residence trust (QPRT) is the present value of the remainder interest at the time of the transfer, which is $450,000. If the grantor survives the 10-year retained term, the residence passes to remainder beneficiaries and is excluded from the estate under Sec. 2036. The annual exclusion does not apply because a remainder interest is a future interest.
